  "status": "constant-mass-block-local-filters-falsified-nonlocal-open",
  "summary": "Proved a Plancherel-incidence no-go for all high-retention block-local isotypic filters. A recurring self-dual retained irrep pairs linearly many good blocks and restores a 2^Theta(k) common family; the next filter must be genuinely nonlocal.",
  "theorem_contract": {
    "common_retained_irrep": "Some alpha is retained on at least qb blocks; every S_n alpha is self-dual.",
    "double_counting": "For N_alpha=#{j:alpha in S_j}, E_{alpha~Plancherel}N_alpha=sum_j p(S_j)>=qb.",
    "locality_no_go": "For q=Omega(1), b=Theta(k), every block-local isotypic filter retaining q Plancherel support has a 2^Theta(k) residual common family.",
    "paired_bypass": "Pair retained-alpha blocks and use one orientation bit per pair. Each alpha tensor alpha membership pattern contains trivial, producing floor(qb/2) common-core bits.",
    "retained_sets": "S_j is the intersection of irrep supports retained on the left and right selected products of good block j.",
    "scope_boundary": "The theorem assumes independent block-isotypic support filters. Growing-block nonlocal, non-isotypic, and global spectral transforms are not covered."
  }
